.page mv 1 move or rename files

# SYNOPSIS
*mv* _SOURCE_ _DEST_
*mv* _SOURCE_... _DIRECTORY_

# DESCRIPTION
`mv` renames _SOURCE_ to _DEST_, or moves the sources into _DIRECTORY_. If the destination is on another filesystem the data is copied (directories recursively) and the original removed afterwards. Words that start with a dash are skipped, so no options are available.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if any move failed.

# EXAMPLES
    mv draft.txt final.txt
    mv *.log /tmp

# SEE ALSO
cp(1), rm(1), trash(1)
